The question was brought up concerning enchanting unicorn horns.
This message also includes info on pick-axes and bullwhips.

SPOILER ALERT


From the code, I determined that unicorn horns (and pick-axes)
enchant like any other weapon:
  If a weapon starts out at > +5 when you read a blessed or
  uncursed enchant weapon scroll, there is a 2/3 chance of it
  evaporating.

Did you also know that this works in reverse?  If a weapon starts
out at < -5 when you read a cursed enchant weapon scroll, there
is a 2/3 change that it will evaporate, too.

As stated previously, unicorn horn do 1-12 damage against both
large and small monsters.  Pick-axes do 1-6 against small monsters
and 1-3 against large monsters.

I also found out that bullwhips have no affect against thick-hided
monsters.  Unfortunately, I don't have a list of which monsters are
considered to be thick-hided.  Then again, at 1-2 against small and
1 against large, who would bother using a bullwhip?



